{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the men took hold.</b> Even though one of them — the one who came to save Lot — was alone in that task, the other, who came to overturn [Sodom], should not have been performing two missions. It is possible to say that since the one who saves, who is Raphael, is the one doing the saving, and Gabriel is only assisting, this is not considered performing two missions. And the reason Gabriel assisted is only to prepare the way for the destruction of Sodom, so that it would not be delayed as long as Lot was still within it, and Raphael was restraining him from doing anything until Lot departed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:22.093465226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}